@startuml sequence_diagram_responsive_keyboard
title WEB02 - SD 3: Use primary navigation and forms at narrow widths
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor "System User" as User
participant "Browser" as Browser
participant AppHeader as Hdr
participant NavigationMenu as Menu
participant RouteOrientation as Orientation
participant FeatureForm as Form
participant FeedbackView as Feedback

User -> Browser : Resize or zoom with a section open
Browser -> Hdr : Reflow sticky shell using available width
Hdr -> Hdr : measureHeight()
Hdr --> Browser : Reserve scroll and focus clearance
Hdr -> Menu : Render the same links in the available space
alt Links overflow
    Menu --> User : Visible primary nav strip and named scroll buttons
    opt User activates a scroll button
        User -> Menu : scrollSections(direction)
        Menu --> User : Scroll list and retain focus on the button
    end
else Links fit
    Menu --> User : All primary links fit in the header
end
User -> Browser : Tab or Shift+Tab
alt Activate the visible-on-focus skip link
    User -> Orientation : skipToMain()
    Orientation --> Browser : Focus main and keep it below the header
else Tab to a navigation link
    Browser -> Menu : Bring focused link into view
    Menu --> User : Clear name and visible focus
    opt Activate link with Enter
        ref over User, Menu : SD 2 - Follow link and orient to the resolved page
    end
end
User -> Form : Edit and submit using labeled keyboard controls
Form -> Form : Keep entered values in the form draft
Form -> Feedback : render(messageKey, values)
Feedback --> User : Show and announce feedback using WEB04 conventions
@enduml
